---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy policy — JAC's Class"
  description="How JAC's Class handles your data, cookies, and analytics."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p style="color: var(--color-muted); font-size: 0.9rem;">Last updated: 27 April 2026</p>

      <p>
        This is the privacy policy for <strong>jaceslclass.com</strong> (referred to as "the site").
        It explains what data the site collects, why, and what your rights are under the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR / RGPD).
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        The site is a static collection of free educational games. There is no account system and no login.
        We collect only what is strictly necessary to operate the site and understand its usage:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Server logs</strong>: IP address, browser, page requested, and timestamp. Held by our hosting provider (Cloudflare) for security and traffic analysis.</li>
        <li><strong>Analytics</strong> (when enabled): aggregated, anonymised page-view data to help us understand which games are most useful.</li>
        <li><strong>Advertising</strong> (if/when enabled): third-party advertising partners (e.g. Google AdSense) may set cookies to serve and measure ads. You will be asked for consent before any advertising cookies are set.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What we do not collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We do not require accounts, names, or email addresses to use the games.</li>
        <li>We do not sell or share data with anyone outside the providers listed above.</li>
        <li>We do not knowingly collect data from children. The site is intended for use by teachers.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        Strictly necessary cookies (e.g. for cookie-consent state) may be set without consent under the GDPR.
        Any non-essential cookies — including advertising and analytics cookies — will only be set after you give consent
        via the cookie banner.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under the GDPR, you have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Access any personal data we hold about you</li>
        <li>Request correction or deletion of that data</li>
        <li>Withdraw consent at any time</li>
        <li>Lodge a complaint with the CNIL (French data protection authority)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        For any privacy-related question, email <a href="mailto:privacy@jaceslclass.com">privacy@jaceslclass.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
